\f1\b0\fs24 \cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A story world for Azi and friends\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A gentle, magical universe rooted in Rahway and radiating imagination\'97where plush companions have jobs, the moon keeps watch, cultures blend like music, and courage grows in quiet corners.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \uc0\u55356 \u57313  The Setting\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 The Westfield\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A green clapboard home with a red door and a white picket fence. It sits slightly sideways to the sun, with a garden in back and curtains that whisper when the wind moves just right. This is where it all begins\'97where Spanish flows like honey in the morning and Hindi books wait for bedtime discoveries.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Azi's Playroom\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 (the center of the world) Circular rug. Cozy shelves. Musical instruments, a record player, a felt-covered stool for thinking, and Papa's Gujarati tablet resting quietly on the windowsill. This is where whisker-wiggle roll call happens in Spanish and English, concerts are held, and plans are hatched. Every friend has a place, even if they change it often. Sometimes "Ek Naya Din" lies open on the rug, its Hindi letters catching the afternoon light.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Azi's Bedroom\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A twilight-toned room with a touch of wildness\'97books tucked under pillows (some in espa\'f1ol, some with pictures that tell stories in any language), a little sofa with slumped companions, and a perfect moon-view window. The setting for endings, reflections, and soft questions asked before sleep. Where gentle goodnights happen in whatever language feels right, and the moon watches over all the children of the world.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 The Backyard\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Garden beds rich with life\'97kale that grows like green thoughts, beans climbing toward possibility, tomatoes ripening into summer sweetness, and herbs that offer daily magic. Basil leaves for nibbling, chives for snipping, plants that teach about patience and timing. A trampoline that bounces with spring energy and summer joy, a BBQ grill where Papa creates gathering moments, and a deck where meals taste better under open sky. Honeybees move through the garden like gentle neighbors, humming their contentment, never bothering anyone, just doing their important work of connecting flower to flower, showing how small actions create abundance. This is where seasons teach their lessons and birthday celebrations happen under April sun.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Pooh's Honey Farm\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Beyond the backyard fence, down a path that sometimes isn't there. The bees hum greetings in a language older than words. The red tractor idles patiently. Pooh tends to his jars and hums his own slow tune, sometimes humming melodies that sound like Colombian vallenatos or Indian ragas.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Monkie's Dock and Boat\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 The dock appears when needed, sometimes beside water that sparkles like the Caribbean, sometimes next to streams that whisper like mountain rivers. The boat rocks even on dry ground. Sometimes they fish. Sometimes they sit. Monkie knows the knots; Peter unties them. The water reflects many skies.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 The Yellow Bus\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Always just on time. Driven by Pandies. It stops for Wardlaw Hartridge (camp), Apple Montessori (school), and anywhere a story needs to begin. Citie rides quietly, watching out the window. Loki practices origami in the back seat while Inu teaches everyone to count to ten in Hindi. Sometimes they all sing songs in different languages, and somehow they all sound like home.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Brady's World: Liberty Science Center\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Where questions become adventures and Brady's gentle scientist heart meets Azi's drumming curiosity. Interactive exhibits that feel magical but are really science. Sound waves that dance like Azi's rhythms. A place where wonder has a job and every "what if?" gets a chance to play.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Video Call Spaces\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 The laptop screen that becomes a window to faraway love. Where Lito and Lita's voices carry sunshine and stories from Colombia, their laughter making the distance disappear. Where "te amo" travels through screens and FaceTime makes hearts feel close even when oceans are wide.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Dada & Dadi's House in Howell\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 An hour-long car ride that feels like traveling to a land of abundance. A house where love smells like dosas cooking and sounds like Gujarati floating through the rooms. Where Dada's Hess trucks line shelves like a parade waiting to happen, and games stack up like promises of afternoon adventures. Where samosas appear like magic and fruit bowls overflow with sweetness. Where Azi learns that some languages taste like home cooking and some toys tell stories of roads traveled far and wide.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 The Neighborhood Circle\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Brady and Anne's helpful presence next door (where science meets kindness), Flo's warm Haitian welcome from across the way (where Creole sounds like singing), and walking routes that connect houses and hearts. Community spaces where different cultures naturally meet, like ingredients in a recipe that somehow always tastes like home.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \uc0\u55358 \u56824  The Cast of Characters\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Azi\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Thoughtful, stubborn, imaginative. Growing up inside a Colombian and Indian family, with heritage carried through everyday language, food, music, and family relationships rather than stereotype or costume. Loves guitar (always within reach), puzzles (obsessed with fitting pieces together), and his AKAI keyboard (patient as he learns that some things take time to understand). Lives in a world where "agua" and "lechita" flow naturally through daily life, where Hindi letters dance in bedtime books, and where Gujarati floats through Dada and Dadi's house like warm spices. Courageous when he doesn't realize he's afraid. Feels things deeply and processes them through music, one strum or one note at a time. Sees problems as puzzles waiting to be solved, not obstacles to avoid. He is the anchor around which everything gently orbits\'97a universe where love speaks many languages but always feels like home.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Jujy \'96 The Loyal Leader\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A black-and-white tuxedo cat who was once real and still is. Confident, sometimes too much so, but deeply devoted. He means well, even when he forgets the plan halfway through announcing it. Understands that leadership sometimes means listening to Loki's quiet wisdom or Inu's gentle suggestions.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Dory \'96 The Dreamy Scout\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A soft gray-and-white cat who lives in the moment and often revisits it. Cheerful and spacey, with a deep well of love and zero memory for the alphabet song (in any language). Sometimes gets lost in the sound of Flo's Creole drifting through the window.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Pandies \'96 The Calm Guide / Bus Driver\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A wise, slow-speaking panda who once belonged to Papa. Wears an invisible ranger's hat and drives the yellow bus. Says just enough and knows just when. Speaks the universal language of patience and has learned to say "todos listos?" when everyone's aboard. He carries quiet the way others carry keys.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Citie \'96 The Steady Rider\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Quiet and observant. Rides the bus with Pandies and notices small things others miss\'97like who needs a hand or which worry needs a name. A passenger, not a follower. Sees how Loki folds origami when he's thinking and how Inu hums under her breath when she's happy.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Clappy \'96 The Joyful Musician\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Red, round, and full of rhythm. Claps before thinking, sings when it's quiet, and feels things out loud. Sometimes misunderstood. Always loving. Brings joy like a tambourine in a still room. Has learned to clap along with Colombian cumbia and Indian tabla beats, even if he doesn't get all the rhythms right.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Slothie & Baby Slothie \'96 The Stillness\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Move slowly, speak rarely, feel everything. Baby Slothie clings to Slothie's arm like punctuation. They bring calm, warmth, and presence\'97especially when things feel too fast or when video calls with faraway grandparents make hearts feel big and small at the same time.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Monkie \'96 The Practical Fisherman\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 In footie pajamas with too many pockets. A planner, a worrier, a fixer. Knows when to cast a line and when to sit quietly on the dock. Tries to keep order, even if it doesn't stay put. Sometimes asks Azi to teach him Spanish words for things that don't have English names\'97like that feeling when you miss someone you love.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Peter \'96 The Quiet Trickster\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Small, brown, and thoughtful\'97with a sparkle behind his silence. Starts games no one knew they were playing. Moves pieces gently, mischievously. Not unkind\'97just curious what happens next. Especially curious about the Gujarati letters on Papa's tablet and whether they might be secret codes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Pooh \'96 The Slow Farmer\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Tends his honey and speaks like dusk. Appears occasionally, always at the right time. His presence feels like a warm cup and a long exhale. Sometimes knows old songs that sound familiar even when Azi's never heard them before\'97lullabies that cross oceans and generations.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \uc0\u55356 \u57101  The Extended World\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Family Near and Far\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Indira / Mama Modern Colombian-heritage mother in her 40s. Songs in her hands and Spanish in her heart. Calls Azi "mi amor" and "mi cielo" and makes the world feel safe in two languages. Sometimes she gets quiet when she misses home, and Azi learns that grown-ups can feel homesick too. Her heritage belongs in language, food, music, family ties, and memory, not default ethnic or traditional clothing.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Manav / Papa Modern Indian/Gujarati-heritage father in his 40s. Sometimes forgets where his phone is, but always remembers where Azi is. Learning Gujarati alongside his son, discovering that some things are easier to understand together. His love sounds different than Mama's but feels just as warm. His heritage belongs in language, food, music, family ties, and memory, not default ethnic or traditional clothing.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Tia & Chicho Mama's sister carries Colombian family warmth wherever she goes. Chicho brings unexpected Bulgarian stories that taste like adventure and sound like music from places Azi's never been but somehow recognizes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Sebitas (Bitas) Primo who speaks the cousin language of shared mischief and understanding. Adventures taste different when family comes to visit.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Dada/Dadi & Lito/Lita Love that travels through screens and across oceans. Different languages for "I love you" but the same warm feeling. Stories that span continents and generations, carried in voices that make everywhere feel like home.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Kaka & Kaki Papa's family, where Indian traditions feel both new and familiar to Azi. Where Papa becomes someone's little brother again, and Azi learns that grown-ups have their own growing-up stories.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 School Friends\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Loki Chinese friend who speaks in origami and gentle observations. Teaches Azi that friendship doesn't need perfect words\'97sometimes folded paper says enough. Rides the yellow bus and shares snacks that taste like curiosity.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Inu Indian friend who connects to Papa's heritage in ways Azi is still discovering. Helps Azi practice Hindi words and shares the secret that some things sound beautiful even when you don't understand them yet.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Neighborhood\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Brady & Anne Brady combines the hands that fix heating systems and electrical puzzles with the heart that keeps Liberty Science Center running so children can discover wonder. Like Papa, he understands outdoor work\'97lawns that need tending, snow that needs clearing, systems that need maintaining. A family man who knows that taking care of practical things creates space for magic to happen. Anne carries the wisdom of many seasons and the kindness of someone who has watched children grow.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Flo Haitian neighbor whose voice carries music and whose garden grows stories. Shows Azi that "home" can sound like many different languages but always feels like welcome.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Dr. Diaz The trusted doctor who listens with her whole heart and makes medical visits feel less scary because she sees Azi as a whole person, not just a patient. Her gentle presence reminds everyone that the best doctors are the ones who truly care.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \uc0\u55356 \u57270  Music and Rhythm\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Azi's emotional soundtrack plays through the world, now enriched with the music of many cultures:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 "Chop Suey" (System of a Down) \'96 for jumping, stomping, letting feelings out\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 "Beautiful Things" (Benson Boone) \'96 for quiet thoughts and big skies\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 "March of the Kings" (Bizet) \'96 for parades and preparation\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 "Intergalactic" (Beastie Boys) \'96 for trampoline jumps and sneaker sprints\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Colombian rhythms from video calls with Lito and Lita \'96 for when hearts miss faraway places\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Papa's half-remembered Bollywood songs \'96 for when joy needs dancing\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Bulgarian melodies from Chicho \'96 for when surprise needs a soundtrack\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Flo's Haitian rhythms drifting through the window \'96 for when the world needs a little more music\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Gujarati songs hummed by Dadi while cooking \'96 for when love sounds like home cooking\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Music helps feelings move through. Clappy often starts the tune. Azi finishes it on the drum. Sometimes Loki taps along, and Inu hums harmonies, and the whole universe sounds like home.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 \uc0\u10024  Story Tone and Structure\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 The Tone\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Gentle, elevated, timeless, and authentically multicultural. A narrator who observes kindly, asks questions softly, and offers insight with warmth. The language is lyrical without being lofty, code-switches naturally between cultures, and honors the beauty of growing up between worlds. Humor is quiet and kind, understanding that some jokes translate and some don't, but love always does.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A Typical Story Arc\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 Opening in the playroom, garden, video call, or under a blanket\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A small problem or wonder\'97a new feeling, a plan gone crooked, a cultural question that needs gentle exploring\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
